<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Bible. It needs none:
  - API keys live in the login Keychain through the legacy SecKeychain API (keyring's
    "keychain" store). That needs no keychain-access-groups entitlement and no provisioning
    profile. Each item's access list names the app's designated requirement (bundle ID and
    team), so later releases signed by the same team read the keys without a prompt.
  - Metal compiles shaders in a system service: no JIT or unsigned-memory exceptions.
  - The app is not sandboxed, so network access and files the user picks need no entitlement.
  - The one framework it loads at run time, Sparkle, is re-signed with the app's team, so
    library validation stays on.
  Add an entitlement only with a note saying which feature needs it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
